  "notes": "ぱさぱさ is an onomatopoeia/mimetic word describing dry, rough, crumbly texture.\n\nUSAGE PATTERNS:\n- ぱさぱさだ: is dry (na-adjective)\n- ぱさぱさしている: is dry (verb form)\n- ぱさぱさになる: to become dry\n\nCOMMONLY DESCRIBES:\n- {髪|かみ}: dry hair\n- {肌|はだ}: dry skin\n- パン: dry, crumbly bread\n- ケーキ: dry cake\n\nCONTRAST:\n- ぱさぱさ: dry, lacking moisture\n- しっとり: moist, supple\n- ふわふわ: fluffy, soft\n- さらさら: smooth, silky (for hair)\n\nNOTE:\nThe voiced version ばさばさ describes rustling sounds or rough/disheveled appearance.",
